WEBVTT

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:19.456
Princess Diana by Anne Collins.

00:00:19.516 --> 00:00:23.347
Published by Macmillan Education.

00:00:23.407 --> 00:00:34.950
A division of Macmillan Publishers Limited, 2009.

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:49.729
Introduction Princess Diana was a very famous British woman.

00:00:49.788 --> 00:00:59.516
In August 1997, Diana was on holiday in the Mediterranean with her new man, Dodie Al-Fayed.

00:00:59.576 --> 00:01:03.540
There were holiday photographs of them in the newspapers.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:06.121
Diana looked happy.

00:01:06.181 --> 00:01:11.376
Then, just a few days later, she was dead.

00:01:11.435 --> 00:01:18.048
She died suddenly on 31 August in a car accident in Paris.

00:01:18.108 --> 00:01:21.860
There are many books about Diana's life.

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:26.082
We often see her photograph and hear her name.

00:01:26.142 --> 00:01:29.143
She was beautiful and famous.

00:01:29.203 --> 00:01:33.545
She was a modern princess and a loving mother.

00:01:33.605 --> 00:01:36.086
She wanted to help people.

00:01:36.146 --> 00:01:39.404
But her life was not always happy.

00:01:39.464 --> 00:01:48.358
This is Diana's story.

00:01:48.418 --> 00:02:05.240
Chapter 1 The Early Years Diana's parents were Francis and Johnny Spencer, the Viscount Althorp.

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:11.971
Johnny was from a very old and important English family, the Spencer family.

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:19.814
George Washington, Humphrey Bogart and Rudolf Valentino were connected to this family.

00:02:19.874 --> 00:02:25.928
Francis was beautiful, but she was also a very strong woman.

00:02:25.987 --> 00:02:31.556
She fell in love with Johnny Ulthorpe when she was only 17 years old.

00:02:31.616 --> 00:02:38.446
Johnny all thought was tall and handsome, and Francis wanted to marry him.

00:02:38.505 --> 00:02:48.579
Johnny went to Eton, one of the most famous private schools in England, and then he was an officer in the army.

00:02:48.639 --> 00:02:53.110
Later he left the army and studied farming.

00:02:53.170 --> 00:03:02.696
Francis and Johnny married on the 1st of June 1954, at St. Margaret's Church, Westminster in London.

00:03:02.756 --> 00:03:05.770
A thousand people were at the wedding.

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:14.076
The Queen, the Duke of Edinburgh, the Queen Mother, and the Queen's sister, Princess Margaret, all came.

00:03:14.136 --> 00:03:19.120
Francis and Johnny lived at Park House in Norfolk.

00:03:19.180 --> 00:03:24.722
The royal family had a house nearby called Sandringham House.

00:03:24.782 --> 00:03:29.016
The royals often came to Sandringham on holiday.

00:03:29.076 --> 00:03:32.786
They knew the Spencer family well.

00:03:32.846 --> 00:03:39.029
When Francis' father died, he left her a lot of money.

00:03:39.089 --> 00:03:46.266
Francis used the money to buy a farm at Snettisham, near Park House.

00:03:46.326 --> 00:03:54.661
In 1955, the couple had a daughter, Sarah, and in 1957, another daughter, Jane.

00:03:54.721 --> 00:04:00.231
In 1960, they had another child.

00:04:00.291 --> 00:04:07.133
This time it was a boy called John, but he died after only ten hours.

00:04:07.193 --> 00:04:13.745
Then, on the 1st of July 1961, Diana was born.

00:04:13.805 --> 00:04:22.477
And three years later, in May 1964, Francis and Johnny had a boy, Charles.

00:04:22.537 --> 00:04:25.860
But there were problems in the marriage.

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:35.027
In 1966, Francis met a new man, Peter Shand Kidd, at a party in London.

00:04:35.087 --> 00:04:38.739
Francis and Peter fell in love.

00:04:38.799 --> 00:04:46.354
At Christmas, 1967, Francis left Johnny and moved to London.

00:04:46.414 --> 00:04:49.625
She wanted to take the children with her.

00:04:49.685 --> 00:04:54.120
Johnny wanted them to stay at Park House with him.

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:57.933
Diana missed her mother very much.

00:04:57.993 --> 00:05:02.144
She was only six years old when Francis left.

00:05:02.204 --> 00:05:09.276
Her sisters were at boarding school, a type of school where they lived most of the time.

00:05:09.336 --> 00:05:15.518
It was a sad and very difficult time for Diana and Charles.

00:05:15.578 --> 00:05:25.564
After Francis left, Johnny paid money to different women, called nannies, to look after the children at Park House.

00:05:25.624 --> 00:05:29.360
The Spencer Children loved Park House.

00:05:29.420 --> 00:05:32.572
It was a large and friendly house.

00:05:32.631 --> 00:05:37.836
Diana loved animals like dogs, cats and rabbits.

00:05:37.896 --> 00:05:44.080
She enjoyed swimming, playing tennis and going for picnics on the beach.

00:05:44.140 --> 00:05:48.895
She visited her mother in London at the weekends.

00:05:48.955 --> 00:05:56.291
Sometimes the royal family invited the Spencer Children to the big house at Sandringham.

00:05:56.351 --> 00:06:02.593
Diana was good friends with Prince Charles' younger brother, Prince Andrew.

00:06:02.653 --> 00:06:08.654
Diana's mother and father divorced in April 1969.

00:06:08.714 --> 00:06:13.345
Francis married Peter Shand Kidd soon after.

00:06:13.405 --> 00:06:18.986
Diana and her brother had holidays with Peter and his three children.

00:06:19.046 --> 00:06:25.729
Later, Francis and Peter bought a big house on the Isle of Sile.

00:06:25.789 --> 00:06:31.084
Sile was an island near the west coast of Scotland.

00:06:31.144 --> 00:06:37.698
Diana went to a small day school near her home called Silfield.

00:06:37.758 --> 00:06:42.550
But when she was nine, her father sent her to boarding school.

00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:46.682
The school was called Riddlesworth Hall.

00:06:46.742 --> 00:06:56.446
In September 1973, when Diana was 12, she moved to another school called West Heath.

00:06:56.506 --> 00:07:01.248
West Heath was near the town of Seven Oaks in Kent.

00:07:01.308 --> 00:07:04.190
Diana liked her new school.

00:07:04.250 --> 00:07:06.892
She had some good friends there.

00:07:06.952 --> 00:07:10.524
She learned to dance and play the piano.

00:07:10.583 --> 00:07:17.908
She was not very interested in school exams, but she was good at dancing and swimming.

00:07:17.968 --> 00:07:22.634
At this time, Johnny Allthorpe met a new woman.

00:07:22.694 --> 00:07:27.718
Her name was Rain Leg, the Countess of Dartmouth.

00:07:27.778 --> 00:07:32.641
Rain was also the writer Barbara Cartland's daughter.

00:07:32.700 --> 00:07:36.562
Rain was married with four children.

00:07:36.622 --> 00:07:44.046
Johnny's children loved their father very much, and they did not want him to be with another woman.

00:07:44.106 --> 00:07:50.978
Then, on the 9th of June 1975, Johnny's father Jack died.

00:07:51.038 --> 00:07:54.338
Jack was the seventh Earl Spencer.

00:07:54.398 --> 00:08:02.702
Now Johnny became the eighth Earl Spencer and Diana became Lady Diana Spencer.

00:08:02.762 --> 00:08:09.906
Johnny and his family went to live in his father's great house at Althorp in Northampton.

00:08:09.966 --> 00:08:14.629
The Spencer children did not like Althorp very much.

00:08:14.688 --> 00:08:18.554
It was a very big house in a large park.

00:08:18.614 --> 00:08:22.312
It had 121 rooms.

00:08:22.371 --> 00:08:27.305
It was a beautiful house, but it was also very cold.

00:08:27.365 --> 00:08:31.138
It was not a home like Park House.

00:08:31.198 --> 00:08:35.080
Rain started to come to Althorpe a lot.

00:08:35.140 --> 00:08:41.144
In May 1976, Rain and her husband divorced.

00:08:41.204 --> 00:08:47.854
Two months later in July, Johnny and Rain married quietly in London.

00:08:47.914 --> 00:08:51.811
Johnny did not tell his children about the wedding.

00:08:51.871 --> 00:08:55.412
They read about it in the newspapers.

00:08:55.472 --> 00:09:00.164
The Spencer children were very angry with their father.

00:09:00.224 --> 00:09:04.046
Now Rain lived at Althorpe all the time.

00:09:04.106 --> 00:09:09.287
Diana loved her father, but he was now married to Rain.

00:09:09.347 --> 00:09:13.093
This was very difficult for Diana.

00:09:13.153 --> 00:09:17.420
Many of Rain and Johnny's friends visited all Thorpe.

00:09:17.480 --> 00:09:19.912
They had a lot of parties there.

00:09:19.972 --> 00:09:25.596
But the Spencer girls were always cold to Rain.

00:09:25.656 --> 00:09:31.170
In 1978, Johnny was very ill and was close to death.

00:09:31.230 --> 00:09:35.612
Rain looked after him and helped save his life.

00:09:35.672 --> 00:09:39.285
Johnny was lucky and he got better.

00:09:39.345 --> 00:09:44.829
But still the children did not like Rain.

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:50.803
Chapter 2 The Prince Prince Charles was born on 14 November 1948 at Buckingham Palace.

00:09:50.823 --> 00:09:51.823
He is the oldest of the Queen's four children.

00:09:51.843 --> 00:10:04.226
He is also the Prince of Wales.

00:10:04.286 --> 00:10:19.823
After the king or queen dies, the prince of Wales usually becomes king.

00:10:19.883 --> 00:10:25.207
So Charles is heir to the throne, or the next king.

00:10:25.267 --> 00:10:29.850
When he was a boy, Charles was very shy.

00:10:29.911 --> 00:10:33.464
He went first to a day school in London.

00:10:33.524 --> 00:10:40.379
Later his parents sent him to Gordonston, a boarding school in northeast Scotland.

00:10:40.439 --> 00:10:44.478
Life for Charles at Gordonston was very hard.

00:10:44.538 --> 00:10:48.956
Charles was sad there and did not have any friends.

00:10:49.016 --> 00:10:52.998
He did not see his parents very often.

00:10:53.058 --> 00:10:57.290
Later Charles went to Cambridge University.

00:10:57.350 --> 00:11:04.344
Then he was an officer in the Royal Navy, the part of the armed forces that works at sea.

00:11:04.404 --> 00:11:07.585
He was in the Navy for five years.

00:11:07.645 --> 00:11:12.090
He was a pilot and flew planes and helicopters.

00:11:12.150 --> 00:11:19.756
Charles enjoyed horse riding and loved playing polo, a game for people riding on horses.

00:11:19.816 --> 00:11:27.270
He also liked hunting and shooting animals, for example birds and deer with a gun.

00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:35.642
When Charles was 23, in the summer of 1970, he met Camilla Shand at a polo match.

00:11:35.702 --> 00:11:39.580
Camilla was 15 months older than Charles.

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:42.603
Camilla was pretty and fun.

00:11:42.663 --> 00:11:45.606
She liked the same things as Charles.

00:11:45.666 --> 00:11:50.970
She loved horses, dogs, the countryside and hunting.

00:11:51.030 --> 00:11:56.334
Charles and Camilla spent weekends together at the home of Earl Mountbatten.

00:11:56.394 --> 00:12:00.458
Earl Mountbatten was Charles's father's uncle.

00:12:00.517 --> 00:12:03.800
Charles was very close to Earl Mountbatten.

00:12:03.860 --> 00:12:06.592
He called the Earl grandpa.

00:12:06.652 --> 00:12:14.578
but Camilla married another young man called Andrew Parker Bowles in July 1973.

00:12:14.638 --> 00:12:18.732
After that, Charles had many girlfriends.

00:12:18.792 --> 00:12:23.536
The newspapers started calling him the Playboy Prince.

00:12:23.596 --> 00:12:27.168
Charles liked tall, blonde women.

00:12:27.228 --> 00:12:37.194
Some of his girlfriends were Divina Sheffield, Anna Wallace and Mountbatten's granddaughter, Amanda Natchball.

00:12:37.254 --> 00:12:41.363
Charles also had friends who were married women.

00:12:41.422 --> 00:12:45.695
One of these was an Australian woman called Dale Trion.

00:12:45.755 --> 00:12:51.458
Her friends called her kanga, like the Australian animal kangaroo.

00:12:51.517 --> 00:12:58.052
But the most important woman friend for Charles was still Camilla Parker Bowles.

00:12:58.112 --> 00:13:03.818
Camilla and Andrew Parker Bowles were now married with two children.

00:13:03.878 --> 00:13:11.677
Andrew Parker Bowles knew about his wife's friendship with Prince Charles, but he was not unhappy about it.

00:13:11.737 --> 00:13:16.340
In fact, Andrew and Prince Charles were friends.

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:19.872
Then something exciting happened.

00:13:19.932 --> 00:13:29.868
Sarah Spencer, Diana's older sister, met Prince Charles at a party at Windsor Castle in the summer of 1977.

00:13:29.928 --> 00:13:33.368
She went to watch the Prince playing polo.

00:13:33.428 --> 00:13:37.109
Later they went on a skiing holiday together.

00:13:37.169 --> 00:13:43.062
The Queen invited Sarah to Balmoral, the royal family's Scottish home.

00:13:43.122 --> 00:13:49.006
That November, Sarah invited Prince Charles to all Thorpe for the weekend.

00:13:49.066 --> 00:13:51.548
Diana was there too.

00:13:51.608 --> 00:13:56.632
She first met Prince Charles in the countryside near her home.

00:13:56.692 --> 00:13:59.908
She was just 16 years old.

00:13:59.968 --> 00:14:06.510
In April 1978, Diana's sister Jane got married.

00:14:06.570 --> 00:14:12.555
Her husband was Robert Fellows, the son of a Norfolk family.

00:14:12.615 --> 00:14:17.128
Later, Robert Fellows had a very important job.

00:14:17.188 --> 00:14:25.146
He was private secretary to the Queen, helping her and working very closely with her.

00:14:25.206 --> 00:14:29.290
Sarah's romance with Prince Charles ended.

00:14:29.350 --> 00:14:37.876
On the 14th of November 1978, the Prince had a dance for his 30th birthday at Buckingham Palace.

00:14:37.936 --> 00:14:42.948
He invited Sarah, but he invited Diana too.

00:14:43.008 --> 00:14:46.882
Diana was very surprised and excited.

00:14:46.942 --> 00:14:50.354
She liked Prince Charles very much.

00:14:50.414 --> 00:14:55.135
Mountbatten wanted Charles to marry and have children.

00:14:55.195 --> 00:15:01.169
Charles usually listened to Mountbatten, but he did not want to get married.

00:15:01.229 --> 00:15:03.722
He did not need a wife.

00:15:03.782 --> 00:15:08.247
He liked painting pictures, and he liked reading books.

00:15:08.307 --> 00:15:10.459
He had his girlfriends.

00:15:10.520 --> 00:15:17.144
He also had servants or people who worked for him to do things for him.

00:15:17.204 --> 00:15:28.518
Then in 1979, the IRA, Irish Republican Army, killed Earl Mountbatten with a bomb in his fishing boat.

00:15:28.578 --> 00:15:35.302
Mountbatten was dead, and Charles was shocked and very sad.

00:15:35.362 --> 00:15:46.118
I have lost someone very special in my life, he said.

00:15:46.178 --> 00:15:57.056
Chapter 3 The fairy story begins.

00:15:57.116 --> 00:16:01.478
Diana was now a young woman of 17.

00:16:01.538 --> 00:16:04.780
She wanted to go and live in London.

00:16:04.840 --> 00:16:08.774
Both her sisters Sarah and Jane lived there.

00:16:08.834 --> 00:16:12.146
They worked for Vogue magazine.

00:16:12.206 --> 00:16:17.130
But Diana was not interested in a job that paid lots of money.

00:16:17.190 --> 00:16:21.232
She loved children and was very good with them.

00:16:21.292 --> 00:16:27.044
So she went to London and found jobs looking after children.

00:16:27.103 --> 00:16:31.214
Diana was very happy with her new life.

00:16:31.274 --> 00:16:39.336
Her mother, Francis, had a flat in Cadogan Square, a very wealthy part of London.

00:16:39.396 --> 00:16:44.058
Diana lived in the flat with two girlfriends.

00:16:44.118 --> 00:16:52.064
In July 1979, her mother bought her a flat in London for her 18th birthday.

00:16:52.124 --> 00:16:57.662
The address was 60 Colhern Court, Chelsea.

00:16:57.722 --> 00:17:01.236
Diana lived there with three friends.

00:17:01.296 --> 00:17:06.890
Caroline Pride, or Caroline Bartholomew after she was married.

00:17:06.950 --> 00:17:10.434
Anne Bolton and Virginia Pittman.

00:17:10.494 --> 00:17:13.326
Diana enjoyed London.

00:17:13.387 --> 00:17:19.515
She did not like parties, but sometimes she went to dances at country houses.

00:17:19.575 --> 00:17:25.362
but she liked sitting at home and watching television with her girlfriends.

00:17:25.422 --> 00:17:34.208
In May 1980, Diana's sister Sarah married Neil McCorkardale, an officer in the Army.

00:17:34.269 --> 00:17:38.852
The married couple lived in Chelsea too, near Diana.

00:17:38.913 --> 00:17:42.055
Diana often went to Sarah's house.

00:17:42.115 --> 00:17:46.948
Sometimes Sarah paid Diana to clean her house for her.

00:17:47.009 --> 00:17:50.691
Diana was now 19 years old.

00:17:50.751 --> 00:17:53.683
She was a happy, pretty young woman.

00:17:53.743 --> 00:17:56.235
Life was good for her.

00:17:56.295 --> 00:18:04.040
Diana met Charles again in July 1980, at a house party in West Sussex.

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:11.516
He invited her to go with him on the Royal Yacht, a large boat called Britannia.

00:18:11.576 --> 00:18:18.236
They were on the boat at cows in the Isle of Wight, an island off the south of England.

00:18:18.296 --> 00:18:25.704
Later, in September, Prince Charles invited Diana to stay at Balmoral in Scotland.

00:18:25.764 --> 00:18:31.877
He invited some other friends too, but they were all much older than Diana.

00:18:31.937 --> 00:18:37.279
Diana's sister Jane and her husband Robert Fellows were there.

00:18:37.339 --> 00:18:41.520
Camilla and Andrew Parker Bowles were there too.

00:18:41.580 --> 00:18:46.067
Charles started seeing Diana more and more.

00:18:46.128 --> 00:18:51.025
The newspapers were very interested in Charles' romantic life.

00:18:51.085 --> 00:18:55.917
Soon they knew all about his beautiful new girlfriend.

00:18:55.977 --> 00:19:01.380
One story in the Sun newspaper said, He's in love again.

00:19:01.440 --> 00:19:05.642
Lady Dye is the new girl for Charles.

00:19:05.702 --> 00:19:16.756
The newspaper reporters, the people who write the stories for newspapers, came to Diana's flat at 60 Colhorn Court in London.

00:19:16.816 --> 00:19:19.106
They waited outside.

00:19:19.166 --> 00:19:23.148
All the reporters wanted to take photographs of her.

00:19:23.208 --> 00:19:26.690
Diana was always nice to the reporters.

00:19:26.750 --> 00:19:30.961
The reporters liked her and became her friends.

00:19:31.021 --> 00:19:36.382
The newspapers started calling her, Shy Die.

00:19:36.442 --> 00:19:42.468
On the 14th of November 1980, Charles was 32 years old.

00:19:42.528 --> 00:19:48.264
The newspapers and Charles' family asked the same question.

00:19:48.324 --> 00:19:52.738
Is Prince Charles going to marry Lady Diana?

00:19:52.798 --> 00:20:00.192
In January 1981, Charles went on a skiing holiday to clusters in Switzerland.

00:20:00.252 --> 00:20:03.836
When he was there, he telephoned Diana.

00:20:03.896 --> 00:20:07.468
I've got something to ask you, he said.

00:20:07.528 --> 00:20:10.336
Diana was very excited.

00:20:10.396 --> 00:20:16.224
She sat with her girlfriend's very late at night, talking about Prince Charles.

00:20:16.284 --> 00:20:21.988
When Charles returned from his holiday, he asked Diana to marry him.

00:20:22.048 --> 00:20:24.710
Diana said yes.

00:20:24.770 --> 00:20:36.043
On the 24th of February 1981, Buckingham Palace told the country that Charles, Prince of Wales, was going to marry Lady Diana Spencer.

00:20:36.103 --> 00:20:41.795
Charles and Diana gave a television interview in the Garden of Buckingham Palace.

00:20:41.855 --> 00:20:46.358
Can you find the right words to say how you feel today?

00:20:46.418 --> 00:20:48.640
asked the interviewer.

00:20:48.700 --> 00:20:55.746
Difficult to find the right sort of words, said Charles, just delighted and happy.

00:20:55.806 --> 00:21:00.010
And I suppose in love asked the interviewer.

00:21:00.070 --> 00:21:03.464
Of course, said Diana Shiley.

00:21:03.524 --> 00:21:08.450
Whatever in love means, Charles answered.

00:21:08.510 --> 00:21:14.295
Two nights later, Diana went to live at Buckingham Palace.

00:21:14.355 --> 00:21:19.560
Most people in Britain were very happy about Charles and Diana.

00:21:19.620 --> 00:21:26.264
People liked reading about Charles' girlfriends, but now it was time for him to marry.

00:21:26.324 --> 00:21:30.240
Everyone was excited about the royal wedding.

00:21:30.300 --> 00:21:35.556
Many people thought that Diana was the perfect wife for Charles.

00:21:35.616 --> 00:21:39.857
She was a beautiful young girl, tall and blonde.

00:21:39.917 --> 00:21:42.238
She was very sweet and shy.

00:21:42.298 --> 00:21:48.840
And, very importantly for the royal family, Prince Charles was her first boyfriend.

00:21:48.900 --> 00:21:55.217
Because of this, the newspapers could not write stories about Diana and other boyfriends.

00:21:55.277 --> 00:21:58.653
Camilla was also happy about Diana.

00:21:58.713 --> 00:22:03.054
Camilla was married and had a husband, Andrew Parker Bowles.

00:22:03.114 --> 00:22:05.664
She could not be Charles's wife.

00:22:05.724 --> 00:22:08.665
But Charles was going to be the next king.

00:22:08.725 --> 00:22:12.756
He needed to have children, so he had to marry someone.

00:22:12.816 --> 00:22:16.336
And Diana was a very sweet girl.

00:22:16.396 --> 00:22:22.816
Diana found her new life at Buckingham Palace, lonely, and a little difficult.

00:22:22.876 --> 00:22:27.408
She had to meet lots of new people and learn new things.

00:22:27.468 --> 00:22:31.322
Charles invited Diana to his friend's homes.

00:22:31.382 --> 00:22:34.364
Often Camilla was there too.

00:22:34.424 --> 00:22:38.508
Camilla often talked to Diana about Charles.

00:22:38.568 --> 00:22:41.461
Diana was very surprised.

00:22:41.521 --> 00:22:44.134
Why was Camilla all was there?

00:22:44.194 --> 00:22:47.862
And how did she know so much about Charles?

00:22:47.922 --> 00:22:53.448
Charles and Diana were married on the 29th of July 1981.

00:22:53.509 --> 00:22:56.000
It was a beautiful summer's day.

00:22:56.060 --> 00:22:59.210
It was a perfect romantic wedding.

00:22:59.270 --> 00:23:06.333
750 million people in more than 70 countries watched the wedding on television.

00:23:06.393 --> 00:23:09.914
Lady Dai was now Princess Dai.

00:23:09.974 --> 00:23:12.616
She was not a shy young girl now.

00:23:12.676 --> 00:23:14.794
She was a princess.

00:23:14.854 --> 00:23:18.022
Diana looked beautiful at her wedding.

00:23:18.082 --> 00:23:22.134
She was in love with her husband, and she was very happy.

00:23:22.194 --> 00:23:26.564
She wore a wonderful, long dress of expensive silk.

00:23:26.625 --> 00:23:32.726
